      "title": "[Dezeen] Why Saudi Arabia's wild giga-project The Line failed",
      "content_html": "<img src=\"http://static.dezeen.com/uploads/2026/10/dezeen-weekly-podcast-9-october-2026-sq_dezeen_1704_col_0-411x411.jpg\" style=\"width:100%;max-height:300px;object-fit:cover;\"/>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 0.75em;padding:5px 10px;background:#f0f4f8;border-left:3px solid #7b9fc4;border-radius:3px;font-size:0.82em;color:#444;line-height:1.8;\">🎨 <a href=\"https://zirnhelt.github.io/super-rss-feed/review.html?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.dezeen.com%2F2026%2F10%2F09%2Fthe-line-neom-saudi-arabia-dezeen-weekly-podcast%2F\" style=\"color:#7b9fc4;text-decoration:none;\">✏️</a></p>\n<p>The world's most wildly ambitious architecture project appears dead in the water. What went wrong? Listen to the latest episode of Dezeen Weekly now. This week, the team plot the strange story of Saudi Arabia's effort to build a linear skyscraper, mega-city in the desert, called The Line. They explain why news that Neom Stadium has</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.dezeen.com/2026/10/09/the-line-neom-saudi-arabia-dezeen-weekly-podcast/\">Why Saudi Arabia's wild giga-project The Line failed</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.dezeen.com\">Dezeen</a>.</p>",
      "date_published": "2026-10-09T09:45:05+00:00",
      "authors": [
        {
