    {
      "id": "https://www.dezeen.com/2026/10/05/mvrdv-barcode-street-furniture-escofet/",
      "url": "https://www.dezeen.com/2026/10/05/mvrdv-barcode-street-furniture-escofet/",
      "title": "[Dezeen] MVRDV designs modular concrete street furniture to be occupied in \"unexpected ways\"",
      "content_html": "<img src=\"http://static.dezeen.com/uploads/2026/10/mvrdv-barcode-street-furniture-escofet_dezeen_2364_col_3-411x411.jpg\" style=\"width:100%;max-height:300px;object-fit:cover;\"/>\n<p>Colourful concrete modules are combined to form impromptu hangout spots in the Barcode collection, designed by architecture studio MVRDV for Barcelona street furniture manufacturer Escofet. The range consists of three basic building blocks – steps, slopes and a joint table and bench – that can be joined together to create an atlas of different topographies.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.dezeen.com/2026/10/05/mvrdv-barcode-street-furniture-escofet/\">MVRDV designs modular concrete street furniture to be occupied in \"unexpected ways\"</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.dezeen.com\">Dezeen</a>.</p>",
      "date_published": "2026-10-05T10:00:46+00:00",
      "authors": [
        {
          "name": "Dezeen",
          "url": "https://www.dezeen.com"
